Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Assertion&nbsp;(A):</strong></td><td>Generally, ionisation enthalpy increases from left to right in a period.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reason&nbsp;(R):</strong></td><td>When successive electrons are added to the orbitals in the same principal quantum level, the shielding effect of inner core of electrons does not increase very much to compensate for the increased attraction of the electron to the nucleus.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="font-size: 1rem;"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;are true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is not the correct explanation of&nbsp;<strong>(A)</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is true but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is false.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>(A)</strong>&nbsp;is false but&nbsp;<strong>(R)</strong>&nbsp;is true.</td></tr></tbody></table>

Given below are two statements:<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:&nbsp;</strong></span></td><td>Generally, only non-metal oxides are acidic but oxides of some metals in high oxidation state are also found to have an acidic character.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:&nbsp;</strong></span></td><td>Oxides like CO, NO, and N<sub>2</sub>O are neutral oxides.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:500px;"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both <strong>statement I</strong> and <strong>statement II</strong> are true.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both <strong>statement I</strong> and <strong>statement II</strong> are false.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct but <strong>statement II</strong> is false.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect but <strong>statement II</strong> is true.</td></tr></tbody></table>
